#
# Strips the agent-session trailer from every commit message.
#
# This repository is public and carries project information only. Some agent harnesses
# append a `Claude-Session:` trailer, and a bare session URL on the line after it, to every
# commit message they write — silently, by standing instruction, so an agent that has been
# told not to do it still does. The history has been rewritten once to remove them and they
# came straight back on the next commit, which is what says the fix belongs here rather than
# in anybody's memory.
#
# `Co-Authored-By:` is deliberately left alone. Who wrote a commit is project information.
# Which private session it was written in is not.
#
# Enable it once per clone — hooks are not checked out active:
#
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks

msg="$1"
tmp="$msg.stripped"

grep -v -E '^Claude-Session:|^https://claude\.ai/code/session' "$msg" > "$tmp"

# Leaves at most one blank line before the trailers, so that removing a trailer does not
# leave the message ending in the blank line that used to separate it.
awk 'NF == 0 { blank++; next } { while (blank-- > 0) print ""; blank = 0; print }' \
  "$tmp" > "$msg"

rm -f "$tmp"
